title: The wire — thread lifecycle and continuability
story: ides-of-march
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: The poet's book-suspicion puts its lifecycle on the scene
  channel — opened, beats, parked, resumed — and its continuability on
  the thread-affordances channel, which clears the moment the talk
  parks and returns when it resumes.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/ides-of-march/chord/ides-of-march.story
    stories/ides-of-march/tests/transcripts/thread-wire.transcript
channels: scene, thread-affordances

---

> north
[OK: contains "Stage"]

> west
[OK: contains "Tiring-House"]

> talk to shakespeare
[OK: contains "The new hired man"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "scene-opened"]

# The book talk opens the thread: lifecycle on the scene channel,
# continuability advertised on thread-affordances.
> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "So it is not carried"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "thread-opened"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "the-suspicion"]
[CHANNEL: thread-affordances, contains "the-suspicion"]

# The poet presses a step further — a beat on the wire, the
# advertisement refreshed rather than stale.
> ask shakespeare about a hired man
[OK: contains "watching what you look at"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "thread-beat"]
[CHANNEL: thread-affordances, contains "the-suspicion"]

> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "the weight of it"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "thread-beat"]

# Steering away parks it — and the continuability clears with it, so
# no consumer renders a parked thread's stale "more to say".
> ask shakespeare about the weather
[OK: contains "pays out line"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "thread-parked"]
[CHANNEL: thread-affordances, not contains "the-suspicion"]

# The return resumes it on the wire, advertisement restored.
> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "You always come back to it"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "thread-resumed"]
[CHANNEL: thread-affordances, contains "the-suspicion"]
